{{Classic Era}}
Once home to one of Norrath's great noble families, Nektropos Castle is now shrouded in tragedy and dark secrets. After years of mistreatment, a servant stole Lord Rikantus Everling's prized enchanted sword and murdered his seven daughters, driving the grieving lord into madness and an obsession with raising the dead. His surviving son, Lord Ollix Everling, desperately seeks to conceal the family's horrifying fate, inviting discreet adventurers into the castle to help preserve its secrets.

Beyond the overgrown lands of [[Lake Nerius]], the castle's locked doors conceal haunted halls, dangerous inhabitants, and the remnants of the Everling family's former glory. Beneath its foundations lies the [[Nektropos Undercrofts]], home to the Ayr'Haeth, a hidden community of [[Half Dark Elf|Half Dark Elves]] whose existence remains unknown to the household above.

Originally featured in EverQuest II as a cursed ruin haunted by the ghosts of the Everling daughters, Nektropos Castle appears in EverQuest Legends approximately 500 years earlier, when the family's tragic history was only beginning to unfold.

